    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nFollowed the existing derived-field pattern (`IdentityKey.of`, `AgeBand.of`, etc.), which keeps structural impact minimal \u2014 a new single-method helper class has zero surrounding complexity to hold.\n\n1. **New class `TelephoneDisplay.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 one static `of(Owner)` method that reads raw E.164 `telephone`, detects the country code (`61`/`1`), and regroups the national digits in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. WMC_other = 0.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` line delegating `telephoneDisplay` to that helper, matching the surrounding lines exactly. No method body grew.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field. `telephone` still stores raw E.164.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` confirms `telephone` = `+61412345678` and `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`.\n\nOne note: the grouping is a generic left-to-right split by threes, so a `+1` 10-digit national number would render as `415 555 123 4`. Only the AU case is exercised by tests and specified by example; if US grouping matters later, that's the spot to refine.",
